id|cell_05
title|The Appointed Day
v_from|31
v_to|48
scenes|scene_08_afghanistan_battle.txt;scene_09_ufo_abduction.txt
beat|The appointed day came. Buyers arrived, sellers arrived, armed men occupied rooftops and alleyways, Kaito's soldiers took their positions, and hidden observers watched from afar; the city grew tense as stillness before a storm. The exchange began; cases were opened, codes verified, payments confirmed. Yet even then there appeared in the heavens above the city a light brighter than any star. Many looked up and pointed in astonishment; others continued their business, believing it some military craft. But the light increased, descended lower, and its shape became visible — unlike any vessel fashioned by the hands of men.

